                        "entry_id": "0e2f2b41-bc00-3557-b5f8-ce487ff10719",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A loiterer; One who goes where he or she does not belong and avoids what he or she should be doing"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f93e6f86-f4de-45ae-a1b4-a7f0230b90c4",
                                "sense_id": "62187d36-08b8-36b3-b50a-1eee9a2103fb",
                                "text": "She went straight into high-sterics, and no wonder; any Christian would, and a Christian Emmeline is, though a meecher from her cradle and will be to her casket."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c35b56c0-a494-46f9-907e-5b7b225e3e0d",
                                "sense_id": "62187d36-08b8-36b3-b50a-1eee9a2103fb",
                                "text": "\"Why,\" he asked, \"have we produced a group of meechers and propagandists, who are Catholics, however nominal, before they are people, and whose principal concern seems to be not to write truly but to win ecclesiastical approbation?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ee73fae-4e96-47e8-b44c-e6406b43307f",
                                "sense_id": "62187d36-08b8-36b3-b50a-1eee9a2103fb",
                                "text": "Uriah Heep is a meecher."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9746820d-909e-47cf-8142-20fddc1ddebd",
                                "sense_id": "62187d36-08b8-36b3-b50a-1eee9a2103fb",
                                "text": "But it did and does seem better to shout a few obvious facts (they can never be 'obvious' enough) than to meech. The meechers will say, Yes, but do you realize all (or any) of the obstacles, presuming you are (in general) a little more right than merely raving?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
